.\" Manpage for timedatectl (timedated bash client)
.TH TIMEDATECTL 1 "June 2026" "timedated" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
timedatectl \- control the system time and date
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B timedatectl
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.IR COMMAND " [" ARGUMENT ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B timedatectl
is a Bash client used to query and change the system clock, the system
timezone, and the settings related to the real-time clock (RTC) and NTP
time synchronization.
.PP
It communicates with the
.B timedated
daemon over the system D-Bus, using the
.B org.freedesktop.timedate1
interface. It is intended as a drop-in replacement for the
.I systemd
tool of the same name on distributions that do not use
.IR systemd .
.PP
Most query commands work as an ordinary user. Commands that change a
setting are authorized through
.IR PolKit ;
depending on the system policy, members of the privileged group (by default
.BR wheel )
may be allowed to perform them without entering a password, while other
users are asked to authenticate.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show the current time settings in human-readable form, including local time,
universal time, RTC time, timezone, and the NTP and RTC flags. This is the
default command when none is given.
.TP
.B show
Show the same settings in a machine-readable
.IB key = value
format.
.TP
.BI set-timezone " ZONE"
Set the system timezone to
.IR ZONE ,
for example
.BR Europe/Athens .
Use
.B list-timezones
to see the available values.
.TP
.BI set-local-rtc " [0|1]"
Control whether the RTC is kept in local time
.RB ( 1 )
or in UTC
.RB ( 0 ).
Keeping the RTC in UTC is generally recommended.
.TP
.BI set-ntp " [0|1]"
Enable
.RB ( 1 )
or disable
.RB ( 0 )
NTP-based automatic time synchronization. Enabling starts and enables the
NTP daemon; disabling stops and disables it.
.TP
.BI set-time " TIME"
Set the system clock manually to
.IR TIME ,
for example
.BR "'2026-05-31 20:30:00'" .
NTP must be disabled first (see
.BR set-ntp ).
The command asks for interactive confirmation before changing the clock.
.TP
.B list-timezones
List all available timezones, one per line.
.TP
.B sync-now
Force an immediate time synchronization. This works even when automatic
mode is disabled: it performs a one-shot synchronization (using
.BR ntpdate ,
falling back to a one-shot
.B ntpd
run), updates the RTC from the corrected system clock, and restarts the NTP
daemon only if it was already running. This command must be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show a short usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Show the current status:
.PP
.RS
.EX
timedatectl status
.EE
.RE
.PP
Change the timezone:
.PP
.RS
.EX
timedatectl set-timezone Europe/Athens
.EE
.RE
.PP
Set the clock manually (NTP must be off):
.PP
.RS
.EX
timedatectl set-ntp 0
timedatectl set-time '2026-05-31 20:30:00'
.EE
.RE
.PP
Recover the correct time afterwards:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo timedatectl sync-now
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and 1 on error (for example, an invalid argument, a
failed D-Bus call, or insufficient privileges).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/localtime
Symlink to the active timezone file under
.IR /usr/share/zoneinfo .
.TP
.I /etc/hardwareclock
Indicates whether the RTC is kept in local time or UTC.
.TP
.I /etc/adjtime
Adjtime configuration used by the RTC handling.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timedated (8),
.BR hwclock (8),
.BR ntpd (8),
.BR date (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Bash client written by Ioannis Anagnostakis (rizitis).
.PP
Part of the
.B timedated
project, a fork of the original Timedate Daemon by Andrey V. Kosteltsev.
